            "descriptor": "Selects one interpretation and repeats its claims without explaining why historians disagree or using specific factual evidence.",
            "exemplar": "I agree with Interpretation 1 because Alan Clark says British soldiers were lions led by donkeys. Haig was an unimaginative cavalryman living in a French chateau while 57,000 men were killed or wounded on the first day of the Somme. He should not have ordered them to walk across No Man’s Land."
